-- title:
--   (3.1), p.4 — bounded martingale increments $|\mathbb E(v_n(0)|\mathcal F_{r+1})-\mathbb E(v_n(0)|\mathcal F_r)|\le 2M/n$
-- statement:
--   Let the game be i.i.d. with $|g_\omega(z,i,j)|\le M$ for all $\omega,z,i,j$, and let $u$ witness orientation. Let $h_1,h_2,\dots\in\mathbb Z$ be levels and let $\mathcal F_r$ be the σ-algebra generated by the payoffs $\omega\mapsto g_\omega(z,i,j)$ with $z\cdot u\in\{h_1,\dots,h_r\}$, $\mathcal F_0$ the trivial σ-algebra. Then for all $n\ge1$ and $r\ge0$,
--
--   $$\bigl|\mathbb E(v_n(0)\mid\mathcal F_{r+1})-\mathbb E(v_n(0)\mid\mathcal F_r)\bigr|\le\frac{2M}{n}\qquad\mathbb P\text{-a.s.}$$
--
--   With $h_1,\dots,h_{Cn}$ the levels of the hyperplanes meeting the cube, $W_r=\mathbb E(v_n(0)\mid\mathcal F_r)$ is a martingale with $W_0=\mathbb E(v_n)$ and $W_{Cn}=v_n(0)$, and this is the increment bound fed to Azuma's inequality.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Conditional expectation is Mathlib's `μ[f|m]`; $\mathcal F_r$ is `levelSigma g u h r`, a supremum of comaps, which is `⊥` at $r=0$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: percolation game with an ergodic measure-preserving ℤ^d-action τ, τ-stationary g, and i.i.d. site vectors (Definition 2.2) → IsIID g μ: each g(z,i,j) measurable, site vectors mutually independent and identically distributed; no τ; reason: i.i.d. site vectors have a translation-invariant law, which is all the proof uses; every i.i.d. percolation game of the paper satisfies IsIID
--   - generalization: ‖g‖_∞ → any M with |g ω z i j| ≤ M for all ω, z, i, j; reason: ‖g‖_∞ is such an M; the statement specializes to it
--   - generalization: levels h_1, …, h_{Cn} of the hyperplanes covering the cube 𝒞; r ∈ [0..Cn − 1] → any sequence of levels h : ℕ → ℤ, any r ∈ ℕ; reason: the argument is the same for every level (a repeated level gives 𝓕_{r+1} = 𝓕_r and increment 0); the paper's choice is an instance
--   - encoding: Γ oriented with the vector u defining H → an explicit witness u with q(i,j)·u > 0; reason: H_r is defined from that u on p.4
--   - encoding: E(·|𝓕_r), 𝓕_r generated by g on ∪_{r′≤r} H_{r′} × I × J, 𝓕_0 trivial → condExp μ[·|levelSigma g u h r], ⨆ of comaps, ⊥ at r = 0; reason: same σ-algebras and conditional expectations
--   - encoding: I and J finite sets → I, J finite and nonempty ([Fintype] [Nonempty]); reason: the max over Σ and the min over T are undefined for empty action sets; only that case is excluded
--   - encoding: ℤ^d; strategies σ_m, τ_m (m ≥ 1) on (ℤ^d × I × J)^{m−1}; max/min in the value → Fin d → ℤ; strategies indexed from m = 0 with Fin m-indexed histories; ⨆/⨅ in `value`; reason: same objects; the families are bounded for every payoff (finitely many reachable histories) and the value is attained (value_eq_minmax)
-- source:
--   Garnier–Ziliotto, Percolation games, arXiv:2110.12227v2, §3.1, display (3.1), p.4, proof on p.5

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_PercolationGames_Model

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Topology

namespace PercolationGames

/-- Display (3.1): bounded martingale increments. Let `u` witness orientation, let `h : ℕ → ℤ` be
any sequence of levels, and let `𝓕_r` be the σ-algebra generated by the payoffs on the hyperplanes
`{z · u = h_k}`, `1 ≤ k ≤ r` (`𝓕_0` trivial). If `|g| ≤ M`, then for all `n ≥ 1` and `r`,
`|𝔼(v_n(0) | 𝓕_{r+1}) − 𝔼(v_n(0) | 𝓕_r)| ≤ 2M / n` almost surely.

Source: Garnier–Ziliotto, *Percolation games*, arXiv:2110.12227v2, §3.1, display (3.1), p.4, with its proof on p.5.

**Formalization Note.** `M` is any uniform bound on `|g|` (the paper's `‖g‖_∞` is the least
one). The levels are any sequence (the paper's `h_1, …, h_{Cn}` covering the cube) and `r` is any
natural number. -/
theorem condExp_increment_le {d : ℕ} {I J : Type*} [Fintype I] [Fintype J] [Nonempty I] [Nonempty J]
    {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (μ : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure μ]
    (q : I → J → Site d) (g : Ω → Site d → I → J → ℝ) (hiid : IsIID g μ)
    (M : ℝ) (hM : ∀ ω z i j, |g ω z i j| ≤ M)
    (u : Site d) (hu : ∀ i j, 0 < dot (q i j) u) (h : ℕ → ℤ)
    (n : ℕ) (hn : 1 ≤ n) (r : ℕ) :
    ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ,
      |μ[fun ω' => value q (g ω') n 0 | levelSigma g u h (r + 1)] ω -
          μ[fun ω' => value q (g ω') n 0 | levelSigma g u h r] ω| ≤ 2 * M / n := by sorry

end PercolationGames
